SPLIT X:BF-L0-0087 | a@31-31: For repeated DELETE of an absent resource choose one convention (204 or 404) and use it consistently. | b@38-38: 304 only for a conditional request whose cached representation is still valid, not a business 'nothing changed'. | c@39-39: 400 for malformed JSON, invalid shape, binding failures and missing transport-level input; not for authentication failure. | d@40-41: 406 when no acceptable representation can be produced; 415 for an unsupported request media type. | e@42-42: 422 for structurally valid but semantically invalid requests, or 400 for both when the project deliberately uses it; follow the established convention. | f@43-43: 428 when a contract-required precondition such as If-Match is absent. | g@44-44: 429 with Retry-After when known for rate-limited requests; never for validation failures. | h@45-45: 500 for unexpected internal failures via centralized handling and ProblemDetails. | i@46-46: 502 only when acting as an intermediary that received an invalid upstream response; not every dependency failure. | j@47-47: 503 with Retry-After when meaningful for temporary inability to serve. | k@48-48: 504 only when acting as an intermediary whose upstream did not respond in time.
RD COMPOUND_PART P:EXTRA-L0-0120 X:BF-L0-0087#a | P: general consistency with the DELETE convention as example.
